    25	## 2. VM design
    26	
    27	### 2.1 Machine model (unchanged)
    28	
    29	The source fragment is literals, variables, let, checked UInt128/Bool primitives, conditional, named call, constructor and ordered match (`design.md:11`). State is control, environment, ordered frames, values, outcome, fuel and counters (`interfaces.md:55-88`). A step is one owner-engine event; helpers in `/1` are explicit bounded microsteps with cursors (`interfaces.md:92-96`). Outcomes: `Running | Halted(v) | Rejected(code) | Exhausted(kind)`. Error codes 4 (frame cap), 9 (no match), 10 (checked arithmetic) are fixed (`interfaces.md:7`).
    30	
    31	Physical layout `sherlock-c6-phys/1`: image header 48 lanes, control 17 lanes, frames 13 lanes each bottom-to-top, sections META/PROG/CTX/IMAGE/DATA/HELPER (`c6_phys.rs:1-30`, `c6_phys_host.rs:1-30`). `StepInv` holds between canonical boundaries: data arena append-only and child-before-parent, frames and helper slots zeroed on release, inactive fields zero (`interfaces.md:177-193`). `decodeCanonical` only at genesis, `ChunkStore`, checkpoint resume and external claims; `decodeStep` mid-run. Internal microsteps preserve `StepInv` without canonical projection (astra-2 SND-002; `security-candidate-b.md:A4`).
    32	
    33	### 2.2 Dispatch (one-hot)
    34	
    35	Today the dispatch owner emits a block for one constant `RuleIdC` and each fragment is its own circuit. In the universal leaf the dispatch is computed once per step:
    36	
    37	1. Inputs: the pre carriers (IMAGE, HELPER, DATA where a value read is gated on, PROG via the parser walk, CTX).
    38	2. Derivation, in the order Core uses (`c6_dispatch_step.rs:9-16`): P0 `outcome == Running`; P1 publication (`Error` control -> `KAdminPublishError`; `Return` at depth 0 -> `KAdminPublishValue`); P2 `remaining_work == 0` -> `KAdminPublishExhausted`; else `owner_select` over helper group, result-reading rule, helper plan entry, legacy group.
    39	3. Output: a one-hot vector `sel[r]` over the supported rule set `R` with `sum(sel) == enable` and each `sel[r]` boolean; `sel[r] == 1` iff rule `r`'s guard path holds. Guard paths include every value read the current per-rule blocks make (for example `equal_differ` reads UInt/Bool/type/constructor values, `c6_dispatch_step.rs:750-806`).
    40	4. Every fragment `F_r` is emitted once and gated: its constraints are multiplied by `sel[r]`, and it produces a candidate post image `cand_r` in which lanes outside its declared write set equal the pre lanes. The step's post image is the selection `post = sum_r sel[r] * cand_r + (1 - sum_r sel[r]) * pre`. Inactive fragments therefore never constrain the shared post image (astra-2 early correction: a `post == pre` constraint under `1 - sel[r]` would block the selected fragment's writes). Test: two rules with differing write sets on the same class, valid differing writes accepted.
    41	5. Two cases are distinct. A *disabled slot* (`enable == 0`, used for padding a short chunk) accepts the constrained identity `post == pre` and contributes zero to `steps`. An *enabled* step whose Core selection is outside the supported set (extension, financial, `XAdtHelperPlan*`, `XAdtHelperBuild*`; `dispatch_supported`, `c6_dispatch_step.rs:29-32`) has no `sel` bit, so `sum(sel) == 0` with `enable == 1` and the leaf refuses (SVM-004).
    42	6. `rules_d` (D5) is the Poseidon digest of the S selected rule ids in order; for S=1 it is the rule id lane the node calls `rule`. The leaf derives `rules_d` and `steps`; `h_pre` is bound by the node to the bounded previous height, not by the leaf (astra-2 lane ownership).
    43	
    44	Soundness premises carried from the per-rule design: canonicality of the pre IMAGE/HELPER/DATA sections is enforced by the gated fragment on the same lanes; PROG canonicality by the parser walk. Putting dispatch and fragments inside one key makes the "caller obligation" at `c6_dispatch_step.rs:34-38` checkable, not discharged: SAS-010 requires, for every admitted rule, evidence that `StepInv` is initialized at canonical genesis, preserved by the gated fragment under `StepInv(pre)`, and that every fragment premise refers to the shared carriers (no disconnected copies). Task 4.6 covers initialization as well as hostile transitions (astra-2).
    45	
    46	### 2.3 S-step leaf
    47	
    48	A leaf proves `S >= 1` consecutive owner steps on one key. Inside the leaf: `pre_0` is the digested `pre_d`; for `i < S-1`, `post_i == pre_{i+1}` lane by lane; `post_{S-1}` is digested as `post_d`. `steps` is the number of *enabled* owner-step events in the leaf; a short final chunk pads with disabled steps (`enable == 0`, identity on lanes, zero contribution to `steps`). Terminal: a step that publishes (`Halted`, `Rejected`, `Exhausted`) is the last enabled step; later slots are disabled. Charged work and fuel stay inside the state digest; `steps` and `h` are physical counts (ISSUE 5).
    49	
    50	S is a keyed constant chosen once at gate G-A (amended 2026-11-08 (3); SRC-014): the rule is `k_U + log2 S <= 20`, with `k_U` the rows of the universal leaf at S=1 (task 4.1, modeling only), so S=8 at `k_U <= 17`, S=4 at `k_U = 18`; S=1 is the one-enabled-slot case of the same relation, not a separate baseline. The leaf is built with S slots (4.2) and keyed once (4.4). With one step per leaf fact(3) is about 293 node proofs at about 95 s each (`stagenet-gp-recursion.md:199-201`); S=8 gives 37 (ESTIMATE 37 x (95 + 47) + 100 = 5,354 s = 1.49 h serial at k_U = 16 and node k=20; `prover.md` §3). Leaf rows grow about S-fold (`k_leaf = k_U + ceil(log2 S)`), prove time about S x t_step, RSS about S x RSS(k_U); the leaf's private witness holds S copies of the carriers; the measured leaf k, time and RSS at the chosen S are recorded at 4.4 (row A20) and the cap is 16 GB per leaf prover so two or three leaf workers fit beside the node under the 100 GB aggregate (open question Q4).
    51	
    52	### 2.4 Identity and configuration
    53	
    54	`prog_d = Poseidon(dom, programImageDigest, layoutSchemaDigest, boundsDigest, profileId)` where the layout schema digest covers `sherlock-c6-phys/1`, `LayoutSchema.recordWidths`, the qualification host config (frames, data, env, value slots) and `Bounds`. A program image under a different layout or caps therefore has a different `prog_d`, and `SherlockRun` seals `program_d` (`sherlock-run.compact:26-47`). This replaces a separate `cfg_d` lane (fable-2 I4; fable-2 critique concession).
    55	
    56	Leaf key identity (manifest): relation id `sherlock-leaf/1`, `sherlock-leaf-stmt/1`, layout schema digest, `Bounds`, ZKIR version (minor read from the compiled `.zkir`), `midnight-zk-stdlib`, `midnight-circuits`, `midnight-proofs` versions, SRS identity, k. The node and decider manifests add the leaf VK digest and the node VK digest respectively (SRC-008).
    57	
    58	### 2.5 Host interface
    59	
    60	`mori simulate` runs the owner engine; `capture(&admitted, &image)` yields a `HostSnapshot` per step; `witness_from_host_snapshot` builds the C6 witness; the witness stream `moriarty-sherlock-c6-witness-stream/1` carries witness, `RuleIdC`, `h_pre`, and digests `prog, init, pre, post` with their `StateOutcome`s (`sherlock_c6_witness_stream.rs`). The stream is the only *application* producer for the leaf prover and the digest-parity test (`sherlock_digest_parity`, commit `3c2657acb`). It is not the oracle: the holdout keeps its independent expected traces (`models/sherlock/oracles/`, `qa/holdout/`) and the hostile-witness suites keep raw witness entry points that bypass the stream (astra-3 early correction). `HostSnapshot` never appears in a public statement; the host supplies private witness only. The public digests `prog_d`, `pre_d`, `post_d` are permitted statement components because the circuit constrains them to the actual witness. Host checks (`checkStepInv`, `ProofPreimage::check`) are diagnostics with no acceptance authority (UISEC-012).
    61	
    62	### 2.6 Fragment coverage
    63	
    64	Gaps at `8fd34ed79`: `KAdminPublishValue`, `BHelperValidate` x4, `BHelperEqual` x4, `BHelperMatch` x10, `BHelperScalarConstruct` (`stagenet-gp-recursion.md:224-243`). WIP source exists (`36456d510`, `5d7663275`) with `native_inventory.rs` rows still `gap(...)`.
    65	
    66	Order (astra-1 early correction, avoids the P3 circularity): first freeze the *admitted rule inventory* `R` for profile `/1` (every supported pure rule, not only the rules P1 and P2 fire), the layout, the caps and the manifests; every rule in `R` has a fragment with a compiled-and-run receipt before the universal leaf is keyed (D9); then P3 is authored from the admitted domain and must need no new key (E2). P1/P2/P3 evidence is finite cross-program evidence, not a proof that every admitted program is sound; the per-rule obligations in `assurance.md` stand beside it.
