   147	
   148	### 5.2 Consequences (SMN-*)
   149	
   150	1. Re-pin and build; `storage 3.0.0` (`Map` keys need `EncodingShape`), `AlignedValueChecked`, fallible cost API, unified signing envelope need source changes in `mori-ledger` and `mori-recursion`.
   151	2. Keygen regression: compute relation and VK hashes for leaf, node, decider, parent and the contract at the new pins; compare with the manifests; regenerate the affected closure in the order leaf -> node -> decider -> acceptRun template -> deploy, because the leaf VK is a node circuit constant (`ivc.rs:10-15`), the node VK a decider constant (`run_decider.rs:5-6`) and the decider VK is installed in the contract; a changed leaf VK changes every key above it. The release note's VK-change classes (zkir V2 `hash_to_curve`; zkir v3 Jubjub-scalar `encode`) are informative only: the node and decider are hand-written `midnight_zk_stdlib::Relation`s on `midnight_circuits` (`ivc.rs:27-45`), not ZKIR, and the leaf is ZKIR v3; the hash regression is the sole discriminator for all four relations (fable-2). Historical keys and receipts stay as historical evidence; they are not declared false (ISSUE 2).
   152	3. Recapture the acceptRun template with 0.36.0; check the 70-lane statement against the public-input limit read from `LedgerParameters`; check the 256-op cap; pay with at least two DUST spends until #838 is fixed.
   153	4. Chain identity = network name + genesis hash + specVersion + ledger rev (SMN-004). Local source/binary provenance and live runtime identity are recorded separately; the deployed node source for spec 2001100 is not public (scout), which is an explicit limit on "exact production reproduction".
   154	5. Deploy `SherlockRun` with a maintenance authority on Preview and on Mainnet (decision 2026-11-08, made by the lead under the owner's delegation "use your judgement on sherlock run"; SMN-007). Reason: the rollback path in `workflow.md` §7 and SWF-010 depends on maintenance key replacement, and the mainnet rollback must be rehearsed on Preview. This is a trust assumption: whoever holds the authority can install a verifier key, so the authority can change what the contract accepts; a `SherlockRun` acceptance is only as trustworthy as the authority holder. The owner holds the authority; its public identity is published in `qa/sherlock/target-pins.json` (no secrets) when the deploy creates it. Every maintenance update is preceded by the A11 keygen regression and produces a committed receipt of the observed on-chain key state; midnight-node #2375 is checked before any key removal. A later change may freeze or renounce the authority once the keys are stable. Inserting a key does not revoke an old one, and redeploying or re-pinning a client does not revoke anything on chain; "retired" is a client-side label until the on-chain key state is observed. A contract holding active state (funds, duties, consumed statements) is never discarded: recovery must migrate or explicitly record the residual exposure; only empty instances may be abandoned (astra-2). Immutable deployment is not chosen for this change; the general rollback rules for contracts without an authority stay in `workflow.md` §7 for earlier or orphaned instances.
   155	6. No stagenet diagnostic call will be made (owner decision 2026-11-08: "not testing on old stagenet"). Stagenet rows stay retired and inspectable as history; no Moriarty row or operation spends wallet or proof-server time on stagenet.
