   110	## Unresolved dissent at consensus
   111	
   112	None. The concerns every member asked to carry forward are recorded as implementation limits, not dissent: the genesis realization must be re-justified at the re-pinned `midnight-circuits 7.3.0` before node keygen (task 2.3; fable-2 prefers realization (b)); the universal soundness/completeness obligations O1-O4 stay open until a theorem exists; the universal leaf k, prover memory for S>1 and complete-path cost are unmeasured; the deployed node source for spec 2001100 is not public (SMN-004 limit). A council vote is not proof execution, deployment acceptance or a release.
   113	
   114	## Owner decisions carried out of the council
   115	
   116	1. Amend `openspec/MORIARTY-COMPLETION-PROGRAM.md:269` (mainnet) or keep M7 blocked.
   117	2. Whether B (Fenrir rollup) rows stay in the factory as non-gating Preview work or are dropped (ISSUE 7: all six accept non-gating).
   118	3. Whether a stagenet diagnostic call is ever worth the wallet and proof-server cost.
   119	4. Whether `SherlockRun` is deployed with a maintenance authority (SMN-007).
   120	
   121	### Resolved 2026-11-08
   122	
   123	The owner's words (2026-11-08, verbatim): "resume the work, merge, amend the program for mainnet, fenrir should test on preview and then mainnet, not testing on old stagenet, use your judgement on sherlock run".
   124	
   125	1. **Resolved 2026-11-08: amend.** `MORIARTY-COMPLETION-PROGRAM.md:270-283` supersedes the `:269` mainnet ban, and the old sentence stays visible struck through. Mainnet submissions are permitted only as T4 operations after local Docker at 9.1.0.1 has passed, the Preview qualification receipts and the Preview rollback rehearsal receipt are committed, and the pre-deploy checklist has passed. Each operation still needs explicit owner authorization when it runs, under an owner-set per-operation spend ceiling with no automatic retry. The amendment authorizes no specific spend (SWF-009, E9, task 7.1).
   126	2. **Resolved 2026-11-08: keep, and make mandatory** (refined by "Resolved 2026-11-08 (2)" below; the Fenrir reading is superseded). The B rows are the required Fenrir path, Preview first and then Mainnet (new rows B4m, B5m, B8m, B9m). They stay outside the Sherlock U023/C4 dependency chain, so Sherlock qualification does not wait on Fenrir. The Fenrir gates (tasks 6.6 and 7.4) depend on them (SWF-013, D14). This replaces the council's "non-gating" outcome for ISSUE 7 by owner decision.
   127	3. **Resolved 2026-11-08: no.** No stagenet diagnostic call will be made, for Sherlock or for Fenrir. The stagenet rows stay retired as history (design §5.2(6), workflow §6).
   128	4. **Resolved 2026-11-08: deploy with a maintenance authority on Preview and on Mainnet.** The owner delegated this decision ("use your judgement on sherlock run"), and the lead made it. Reason: the rollback path (`workflow.md` §7, SWF-010) depends on maintenance key replacement, and the mainnet rollback must be rehearsed on Preview. This is a trust assumption: whoever holds the authority can install a verifier key, so the authority can change what the contract accepts. The owner holds the authority; its public identity is published in `target-pins.json`. Every maintenance update is preceded by the A11 keygen regression and produces a committed receipt of the observed on-chain key state; midnight-node #2375 is checked before any key removal. A later change may freeze or renounce the authority once the keys are stable (SMN-007, design §5.2(5), `tasks.md` "Later changes").
   129	
   130	### Resolved 2026-11-08 (2)
   131	
   132	The owner's words (2026-11-08, verbatim): "Sherlock should not depend at all on Fenrir, We have a synthetic rollup design, we use that".
   133	
   134	The owner's words on the C4 closure (2026-11-08, verbatim): "keep them out of C4".
   135	
   136	This refines decision 2 above ("fenrir should test on preview and then mainnet"), which commit 927f12956 applied by making the Fenrir B rows required, Preview then Mainnet.
   137	
   138	1. **No Fenrir dependency.** Moriarty and Sherlock carry no dependency on Fenrir: no Fenrir-owned gate, row, operation, file, repository or live Fenrir system (SWF-014, D14). Fenrir's own testing on Preview and Mainnet belongs to the Fenrir project, not to Moriarty's predicates.
   139	2. **The B rows are Sherlock's synthetic rollup.** The B rows keep their IDs and become Sherlock's synthetic-rollup qualification on data that FSYN generates in this repository (`openspec/changes/sherlock-synthetic-rollup-data/`, SSRD-029, SSRD-030): local first (B1, B2, B3, B6, B7), then Preview (B4p, B5p, B8p, B9p; OP-PV-SYNTH-ROLLUP), then Mainnet (B4m, B5m, B8m, B9m; OP-MN-SYNTH-ROLLUP). OP-PV-FENRIR-BATCH and OP-MN-FENRIR-BATCH are renamed accordingly (SWF-013, tasks 6.6 and 7.4).
   140	3. **Outside C4, by owner decision.** The earlier reason for keeping the B rows out of the C4 closure ("Sherlock should not wait on Fenrir") no longer applies, because the rows are Sherlock's own work. The owner decided to keep them out of C4 ("keep them out of C4"). C4 stays the Sherlock M6 gate for representation and arithmetic on P1-P3; the synthetic-rollup gates (tasks 6.6, 7.4) depend on the B rows.
   141	4. **Stagenet stays retired.** B4, B5, B8 and B9 stay retired; decision 3 above is unchanged.
   142	5. **Code decoupling is separate.** B1, B2 and B3 (and through B3, B6 and B7) still read a Fenrir checkout today; their rows record this. Task 1.9 replaces every such read with FSYN-generated in-repository fixtures and adds the T0 guard F17. The synthetic rollup change is amended so that FSYN is self-contained, its design-cut constants are restated as Moriarty-owned parameters, and sync with Fenrir is optional, offline and manual (its proposal, "Owner amendment 2026-11-08").
   143	
   144	### Resolved 2026-11-08 (3): the speed re-plan
   145	
   146	The owner's words (2026-11-08, verbatim), in the order they were given:
   147	
   148	- On the measured recursion (293 node steps at about 95 s each, 7.7 h for fact(3)): "way too slow".
   149	- On the proposal to re-plan: "yes, re-plan it, and reopen tree aggregation and allow the planning agents to search online for ideas".
   150	- On the design method: "whatever approach you choose have some agents explore it with lean and quint to reason about its design. It has to be general purpose recursion".
   151	- On memory: "yes, 48 GB per process, 100 GB aggregate".
   152	- On tooling: "use the tools in the workflowskills repo".
   153	- On installs: the Lean toolchain (v4.33.1; `clean/fork` SherlockSpec builds) and CUDA 13.4.3 (`/opt/cuda/bin/nvcc`) were approved and installed on 2026-11-08.
   154	- On the GPU, after the planning agents reported that ICICLE's CUDA backend is closed source and licence-server gated and that sppark supports no ARM64 GPU host: "you'll have to build one in rust. Search online for CUDA rust kernels for these things".
   155	
   156	The three planning reports are `research/sherlock-speed-replan-20261108/{tree,prover,order}.md`; the lead's synthesis is this amendment. What was decided:
   157	
   158	1. **Throughput is mandatory.** SRC-011 moves from Optional to Ubiquitous with the owner's caps: under 2 h wall, under 48 GB peak RSS per process, under 100 GB aggregate across the concurrent heavy processes of a run; a shortfall is a failing row, never a pass by being recorded. This supersedes the ISSUE 9 reading ("shortfall reporting closes measurement only") in the stronger direction: the measurement tasks still close on a recorded shortfall, but the throughput rows (A18, A19, A19b) then fail and gate G-C blocks OP-PV-DEPLOY. Staged gates SRC-015: node step at k=19 <= 60 s / 16 GB (A16), `entry 7;` under 20 min (A18, G-B), fact(3) and list123 under 2 h (A19, A19b, G-C). Caps are seeded requirement caps (`fixed: true`), not measured-then-doubled.
   159	2. **Memory safety first (SRC-016, task 2.0, E11 required).** The 112-117 GB `mori_backend` test binary of 2026-11-08 ran with no memory guard (`order.md` §1 item 1). Every heavy process runs under a kernel cgroup cap of at most 48 GiB with swap off; a declared concurrent run sits in a 100 GiB parent scope; preflight checks `MemAvailable` and swap; the aggregate admission rule is enforced by the queue; heavy tests are `#[ignore]` in plain `cargo test` and `RUST_TEST_THREADS <= 4` for the prover crates. E11 (heavy concurrency) moves from "named, not planned" to task 2.0 of this change. No heavy run before F18.
   160	3. **Primary path: S-batched linear IVC with parallel leaf workers.** Leaves are independent, so 2-3 leaf workers prove ahead of the node chain under the 100 GB aggregate; the node is trimmed to k=19 inside task 2.3 so that 2.4 keys once; the thread sweep is lever 0; S is a keyed constant chosen once (provisionally at G-A from the node numbers, finally at G-A' from the measured `k_U`) by `k_U + log2 S <= 20`, and the leaf is built with S slots and keyed once (SRC-014 unconditional; SRC-013's rule becomes `k <= 17 + log2 S` at the keyed S, and option F fixes S=1). This supersedes the ISSUE 6 conditions ("S=1 as the initial qualified baseline", "S=8 an experiment"): the measured-first principle behind them is kept (`k_U` is measured before S is fixed, and S=1 remains the one-enabled-slot case of the same relation), but S is no longer an after-the-fact experiment that would cost a second key cascade.
   161	4. **Tree aggregation reopened as a measured option (D13').** The uniform three-slot self-recursive node of `tree.md` F8 (one key, disabled slots the identity, hash-bound manifest) replaces the cut binary tree; the per-level-key fallback of `stagenet-gp-recursion.md:168` is struck because it violates the fixed-key requirement. The tree is decided at G-A and G-B by `tree.md` §7 and `prover.md` §6: it is the lever if `k_U >= 18` or k=19 fails, or if the chain alone misses the target. Its criterion 3 (the owner amends SRC-011 to a 100 GB aggregate and funds E11) is met by this decision.
   162	5. **One general aggregation model (SRC-017).** Segment composition is modeled once, the linear chain being the degenerate tree: a Quint model (`models/sherlock/quint/aggregation.qnt`, constants `TREE` and `S`, F20) and Lean theorems (`clean/fork/Clean/Sherlock/Aggregation.lean` in `SherlockSpec`, F21) cover linkage and associativity, padding and identity neutrality, exactly-once coverage, height bounds, unique genesis, replay, schedule independence, program fixity, shape binding, independence from shape and S, and "the root statement implies a valid execution of the general machine for every program". One fixed key set serves every program and every step count. The tools are the `quint-modeling`, `quint-lang` and `quint-execute-spec` skills and the lean4 plugin of the workflowskills repo. A council review (skill `council`, cross-family lanes; task 2.14) of the design plus the formal results precedes the implementation of the node constraints (2.3), the S-slot leaf (4.2) and any tree node (5.7).
   163	6. **GPU: an open-source Rust MSM/NTT build, phased, optional (SRC-018, design §3.7).** No ICICLE or sppark crate dependency (closed CUDA backend, licence-server gated; no ARM64 GPU host support). Source code borrowed into `crates/mori-gpu` is allowed only under MIT or Apache-2.0 (owner decision 2026-11-08 (4), below). Phases: toolchain smoke on sm_121 (done 2026-11-08: a 64-bit `mulhi` kernel matched the CPU) -> field kernels -> MSM -> NTT -> prover integration behind a default-off `gpu` feature of a patched `midnight-proofs 0.8.3` -> node-step measurement; each phase has a kill criterion and a time box; the track opens past the smoke only when the C0 MSM-plus-NTT share is at least 0.4; proofs stay byte-identical under the stock Midnight verifier. The design source is `research/sherlock-speed-replan-20261108/gpu.md` (`crates/mori-gpu`).
   164	7. **New task order (tasks.md).** 2.1 -> 1.9 -> 2.0 -> the C0 path (2.7, 2.8, 2.9, 2.13) and the formal tasks (2.11, 2.12) in parallel -> 2.14 -> G-A -> 2.3 -> 2.4 -> 2.5 -> 2.6 -> GPU phases if open; M4 chooses S at G-A' before the leaf is keyed; M5 carries the throughput gates G-B and G-C; 6.2 depends on G-C. Each task is marked **[loop]** (unattended), **[lead]** (gate or decision) or **[owner]** (install or spend). Gate decisions are committed JSON under `qa/sherlock/decisions/` (`speed-levers.json`).
   165	
   166	No council member dissented from this amendment; it was an owner decision outside the council round, and the measured-first conditions of ISSUE 6 and ISSUE 9 are preserved as described in items 1 and 3.
   167	
   168	### Resolved 2026-11-08 (4): borrowed GPU kernel code
   169	
   170	- Asked whether CUDA C++ kernel templates adapted from sppark (Apache-2.0) or ICICLE v2.8.0 (MIT) inside the Rust crate satisfy "you'll have to build one in rust", the owner said (verbatim): "I don't care as long as the license is MIT or Apache2".
   171	- Carried out: code borrowed into `crates/mori-gpu` or `tools/gpu-prover/` SHALL be MIT or Apache-2.0 licensed, keep its licence and copyright headers, and be recorded with source URL and commit in the crate's provenance notes. Code under any other licence (MPL-2.0, GPL, no licence, or ICICLE v3+ terms) SHALL NOT be copied. A crate dependency on ICICLE's closed CUDA backend stays excluded. This settles gpu-align finding (a); `gpu.md` §2 already follows it.
   172	
   173	### Resolved 2026-11-08 (5): the target is Mainnet, tested on Preview
   174	
   175	- The owner said (verbatim): "We don't care about stagenet anymore, Midnight forked, this can work on mainnet. We should test on preview or preprod (whichever is the canonical test infrastructure)."
   176	- Carried out: the goal of this change is Sherlock on Midnight Mainnet with full general-purpose recursion. Stagenet is not a target (decision 3 of "Resolved 2026-11-08" already retired it).
   177	- The test network is Preview. Preview runs ledger 9.1.0.1, the same as Mainnet, as a new chain since 2026-11-07. Preprod still runs ledger 8.1.3, and toolchains 0.34-0.36 cannot deploy to it (`wiki/midnight-ledger-9-hardfork.md`, support matrix). The order stays: local Docker at 9.1.0.1 (`undeployed`), then Preview (M6), then Mainnet (M7). If Preprod moves to ledger 9, a later change may add Preprod rows; this change adds none.
   178	
   179	### Owner decisions still open after 2026-11-08 (3)
   180	
   181	1. Whether to fund the GPU build phases (2.10b-2.10f; agent time, each time-boxed) if gate G-A opens the track (`m + q >= 0.4`). Without that decision the track closes at the smoke and the GPU rows stay optional.
   182	2. Whether to fund the tree build (task 5.7; `tree.md` ESTIMATE 1-2 weeks) if gate G-A opens it, when the chain at the chosen S is projected to miss 2 h.
   183	3. If `k_U > 17` forces option F (S=1), whether the 2 h target may rest on k=19, concurrency, the GPU and the tree alone, or whether the inventory `R` or the leaf design is revisited first.
   184	4. Items 1-4 of the earlier lists stay as recorded (stagenet, maintenance authority, mainnet spend); any spend remains an owner authorization per operation.

