   176	
   177	### C5 (high). "General purpose recursion" is narrower than the text. §3.6, SRC-017, 4.3, 4.4, M6.
   178	
   179	What the code gives:
   180	- One key set for every Sherlock program **inside one frozen inventory, layout, `Bounds`,
   181	  profile and S**. `Bounds` and the layout are part of the leaf key identity (`D/design.md:54-56`);
   182	  the leaf key is a node constant (`ivc.rs:575`) and the node key a decider constant
   183	  (`run_decider.rs:206-216`). The qualification config is sized to P1-P3
   184	  (`docs/sherlock/stagenet-gp-recursion.md:162-163`). A program that needs more capacity needs a
   185	  new key closure and a new contract key. The full-carrier hash grows with carrier length, so
   186	  larger `Bounds` add leaf work; there is no design for large states.
   187	- Sherlock leaves only. The node verifies one fixed leaf key and itself (`ivc.rs:548-562`);
   188	  linked segments share one `prog_d` (`Aggregation.lean:49`). Nothing aggregates a proof of
   189	  another circuit or of two programs. That needs authenticated circuit identity, a key policy
   190	  and statement adapters: a different design.
   191	- Only `Halted` with a u128 result is accepted (`run_decider.rs:278-288`;
   192	  `crates/mori-backend/src/sherlock_c6_witness_stream.rs:138-158`). `Rejected`, `Exhausted` and
   193	  structured results have no path.
   194	- One contract per sealed `(program_d, init_d)` (`sherlock-run.compact:25-26,40-47`), and no
   195	  run-input interface (`sherlock_c6_witness_stream.rs:170-177`). Under the soundness premises the
   196	  Lean uniqueness result (`Aggregation.lean:1136`) means at most one valid `stmt` per contract.
   197	- "Any shape" is the linear chain in practice. The tree is a different node statement and key
   198	  (`D/tasks.md:83`), and it is closed; `D/design.md:79` "the statement, decider and `acceptRun`
   199	  are the same" is too broad.
   200	- Runs of at least one step (`ivc.rs:359-372`).
   201	
   202	Proposed change: restate SRC-017 and §3.6 in three scopes (admitted Sherlock programs; other
   203	aggregation shapes for Sherlock segments; arbitrary-circuit aggregation as a separate
   204	extension), and put one owner question before the Mainnet deploy: which of run input, a registry
   205	contract taking `prog_d` as an argument, non-halted outcomes, and foreign proofs are in scope.
   206	Run input is not a template-only change: it needs admission, initialization, binding and witness
   207	production.
