   124	Route (gpu.md F1, §2, ranked): a Rust crate `crates/mori-gpu` (main workspace member; feature `cuda` default off; no `midnight-proofs` dependency) whose `build.rs` runs nvcc 13.4 (`-gencode arch=compute_121,code=sm_121`, plus `compute_120` PTX for portability; `MORI_GPU_ARCH` overrides) over a small CUDA C++ core (`cuda/field.cuh`, `curve.cuh`, `msm.cu`, `ntt.cu`, kept under about 2,000 lines) into a static library linked with `cudart`; the algorithm, dispatch, SRS cache, fallback, receipts and tests are Rust. Every pure-Rust kernel route is blocked on sm_121 today (Rust-CUDA needs a nightly and libNVVM; cuda-oxide 0.3.0 lists sm_80..sm_120a and has no mul-hi; CubeCL is alpha; rust-gpu/wgpu have no u128); a port of the kernels to one of them, with the same tests and hooks, is the migration target once one verifies sm_121 with u64 `mul_hi` on stable (gpu.md Q7). The owner's "build one in Rust" is met by owning the whole backend in a Rust crate with a small, tested CUDA core; `cudarc` is optional (NVRTC, stream wrappers), not required. Kernel sources: sppark's field, XYZZ curve and NTT templates (Apache-2.0) and the Yrrid/Snarkify ZPrize-2023 BLS12-381 MSM plan (MIT/Apache-2.0: signed 22-bit windows, sorted buckets, precomputed multiples); fallbacks ICICLE **v2.8.0 tag** (MIT) and ec-gpu (MIT/Apache), headers preserved. **Excluded**: ICICLE v3+/open-icicle CUDA backends (closed or conflicting licence), polytope-labs/gnark-cuda and the td-kwj WebGPU MSM (no licence file), Nocy's proof server (no licence), Snarkify's ZPrize-1B code (MPL-2.0). sppark and ICICLE enter as borrowed template source with attribution, never as crate dependencies (sppark declares ARM64 GPU hosts unsupported; ICICLE's current backend is licence-server gated).
   125	
   126	Integration (gpu.md F6, §3): `msm_specific` and the `EvaluationDomain` transforms are free functions with no trait seam, and `KZGCommitmentScheme<Bls12>` is baked into the keys and gadgets, so the seam is two registries in a patched `midnight-proofs 0.8.3` (`hooks::MSM_G1: OnceLock<fn(&[Fq], &[G1Projective]) -> G1Projective>`, `hooks::FFT_FQ: OnceLock<fn(&mut [Fq], Fq, u32)>`, about 60 lines, inert when nothing is registered; `Fq`/G1 specialisations only). The patch lives in a **separate workspace `tools/gpu-prover/`** (own `Cargo.lock`, vendored `vendor/midnight-proofs-0.8.3-gpu` = registry 0.8.3 + `patches/gpu-hooks.diff`, SHA-256 checked, `[patch.crates-io]` local to that workspace; the shape of `tools/profile/`), because a `[patch.crates-io]` in the main `Cargo.toml` would rewrite `Cargo.lock` for every consumer of `midnight-proofs 0.8.3` (RPP-007; `order.md` §5.8). Its `heavy --gpu` entry calls `mori_gpu::install()` to register the hooks and then the same mori-recursion / mori-backend APIs as the CPU path. The main workspace keeps the registry crate; `scripts/qa/check-profile-isolation.py` is extended to the second vendored copy. Fallback has three levels (compile-time `cuda` off; init-time `cudaGetDeviceCount` fails or `MORI_GPU=off`; call-time `n < 2^MORI_GPU_MIN_K` (default 14) or a kernel error), each with the CPU result and a `fallbacks` count in the receipt; the GPU is never a correctness dependency. Receipts: `runs.jsonl` rows gain `gpu: {arch, driver, toolkit, msm_calls, ntt_calls, fallbacks, device_bytes_peak}`. Per GPU prover the device-side footprint is 1.5-2.5 GB (affine SRS tables 2 x 96 MB at k20, optional precompute up to 1.5 GB, NTT scratch 2 x 256 MB, MSM scratch ~0.3 GB, twiddles 0.13 GB, context ~0.3 GB), counted inside the 48 GB cap and the 100 GB aggregate; concurrent `heavy --gpu` processes take `gpu.lock` or share by time-slicing (measured at G6). General-purpose rule: the backend takes any `n <= SRS size` and any `log_n <= 32`; nothing in it knows the program or the circuit; the SRS cache is keyed by content.
   127	
   128	Bit-identity (gpu.md F5, §0): points reach the transcript as 48-byte compressed encodings, so for the MSM "bit-identical" means **group equality** with BLST's result, checked on `to_affine()` and compressed bytes (different projective (X, Y, Z) for the same point is fine); the NTT must be bit-exact per element; proof bytes must be equal. Edge classes: identity point as base and as result, zero scalars (filtered before the call, but accepted by the kernel), duplicate bases (the XYZZ mixed add is incomplete at P = Q and must branch to a doubling), the signed-digit exceptions (digit -2^(c-1), top-window carry, scalars 1 and r-1), projective bases with Z != 1, and host- versus device-resident inputs (the ICICLE/gnark Montgomery-chunking bug class). If the prove API draws blinding from `OsRng` only, A27 degrades to "verifies and every commitment equal given logged blinding", stated in the receipt (gpu.md Q4); a seedable RNG entry through the test harness is preferred.
   129	
   130	Phases (gpu.md §6; estimates and kill criteria are gpu.md's): **G0 toolchain smoke, done** 2026-11-08 (F23, task 2.10a; nvcc sm_121 kernel at 21:57; a Rust `build.rs` -> nvcc -> static lib -> kernel on plain `Vec<u32>` memory, 65,536 8-limb products, 0 mismatches, 367 ms with context creation); **G1 source compile** (sppark `poc/msm-cuda` for BLS12-381 and its `ntt` test at `-arch=sm_121` on this aarch64 host, 2^16 vs BLST; kill: no compile after 2 working days -> ICICLE v2.8.0 or Yrrid sources, and if none compiles write `field.cuh` ourselves, +1-2 weeks; 2-4 days); **G2 field kernels** (A24: `field.cuh`, `curve.cuh`, unit tests vs blst; gate: tests pass and Fp mul >= 2 G/s on a 2^24 micro-benchmark; kill < 1 G/s after tuning; 1 week); **G3 MSM** (A25: 2^20 random MSM <= 100 ms (BLST 0.51 s, >= 5x) and every differential test group-equal, `MIN_K` measured; kill > 250 ms at 2^20 (< 2x) after two tuning rounds; 2-3 weeks; ESTIMATE 50-90 ms = 6-10x, 15-25 ms with precompute factor 8); **G4 NTT** (A26: 2^23 <= 40 ms and 2^20 <= 5 ms, bit-exact; kill > 200 ms at 2^23 (< 2.5x); 1-2 weeks; ESTIMATE 2^20 2-3 ms = 25x, 2^23 15-25 ms = 20-30x, the CPU FFT being bandwidth-bound on the same bus); **G5 integration** (A27: `tools/gpu-prover/`, hooks patch, `heavy --gpu`, receipts, isolation check; gate: proof byte-identity on the `entry 7;` node, one leaf (k13, below `MIN_K`: exercises the fallback) and the decider, stock verify, T0 isolation; kill: a byte mismatch not explained and fixed within a week -> hold at CPU; 1-2 weeks); **G6 node-step measurement** (A21: `gpu-msm-node-step`, node k20 (and k19 once cut) with 0, 2 and 3 leaf workers beside it; gate: `node_step_wall` improvement >= the C0 Amdahl bound - 20%, per-process RSS including device <= 48 GB, aggregate <= 100 GB; kill < 1.2x -> GPU row closed, crate kept for later pins; 2-3 days). Gates with the rest of the plan: the track opens past G0 only when G-A records m + q >= 0.4 (Amdahl bound >= 1.67x) **and** the owner funds the phases (`dissent.md` "Open for the owner" 1); within the track, G3 is justified by the MSM share (`order.md` table 2.5: m >= 0.45 after k19) and G4 by the NTT share (gpu.md §4.2: q >= 0.15, bound >= 1.18x), so one of them may run without the other; G5 waits for the post-2.1 pins to settle so the patch is cut once; fuzzing (`cargo fuzz` targets `msm_diff`, `ntt_diff`, nightly 30 min under `gpu.lock`) starts at G3. Node-step ESTIMATE at GPU factors 7x (MSM) and 15x (NTT): 2.65x at m = 0.4, q = 0.3; 1.55x at m = 0.25, q = 0.15; smaller at k = 19 because the fixed phases do not shrink, and the next ledger pin (#350 affine SRS, #352 pruned DIF FFT) speeds up the CPU baseline. Proofs stay byte-identical; keys, VKs and the format do not change.
   131	
   132	Assurance (gpu.md §5): differential MSM tests vs `multi_exp` and, for n <= 2^12, a naive sum (n in {1, 2, 3, 2^k, 2^k +- 1} for k in 10..=21 and the edge classes above); differential NTT tests vs `best_fft` for log_n in 1..=23 (omega and omega_inv, structured vectors, round trip, coset transforms through the patched `EvaluationDomain` vs the registry one); proof byte-identity (A27); kernel unit tests vs blst (10^6 random pairs plus 0, 1, p-1, R, R^2; XYZZ add/dbl on random, equal and identity points; recode vs a Rust reference); fuzzing; and two small formal targets labelled per SAS-009: a Quint model of signed-digit Pippenger over a small abstract group (recode with carries, bucket accumulation, running-sum reduction, Horner; invariant result = sum s_i P_i including digit -2^(c-1), the top-window carry, zero digits and duplicate indices) plus the NTT index permutation (three bit-sliced passes compose to `best_fft`'s bit reversal, Quint or proptest), and Lean lemmas for the digit-recoding identity (`sum d_i 2^(c i) = s`, d_i in [-2^(c-1), 2^(c-1)], all s < 2^255) and the completeness of the XYZZ mixed-add case split (P = Q, P = -Q, identity operands). None of these may pass vacuously on a GPU-free host; they run on this host under `gpu.lock`.
