openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/tasks.md:40:- [x] 2.3 **Node fixes and the k=19 cut in one change** (amended 2026-11-08 (3); depends F20, F21 and 2.14): range checks on `prev_h`, `steps`, `h` (`ivc.rs:308-310`, pattern `parent.rs:665-670`); `steps <= S_MAX` with `S_MAX` a relation constant equal to the G-A provisional S (16 unless G-A says otherwise; 4.4 keys the final value); genesis per SRC-005: select realization (a) neutral-encoding constraint or (b) zero/ignore construction with a recorded justification (an unscaled retained carry needs its own security argument; the `24a1eb5a` hash observation is an input, not the argument), confirm at `midnight-circuits 7.3.0`, record the choice before node keygen; the node's `fold` matches the Quint model's `fold` (F20) and the `Leaf`/`link` of the Lean theorems (F21); then the row cut to `cost_model` k == 19 with the fixes in (Q9: where the 7,701 excess rows are, per-gadget row report; candidates `prover.md` §2: `nr_pow2range_cols` 3 vs 4, the leaf-instance lanes `rule`/`binding` folded into `rules_d`, accumulator assignment width; the SRC-004 checks add only 30-50 rows); if rows cannot get under 2^19 without an arch change, keep k=20 and record it for G-A (S and the tree then carry the target). Negative tests at the constraint boundary with a valid baseline and through the final pairing. T1 check: `SherlockIvcRelation::new(4, 19, leaf_vk)` and `cost_model(&r, Some(19)).k == 19`. [SRC-003, SRC-004, SRC-005, SRC-015, SRC-017] -> A13 (prerequisite), A16 **[loop]** T1 check and negatives, **[lead]** the cut Input 2026-11-08 (`1edd79146`, SHKIVC05): the node never verified after SHKIVC03 (every node proof failed `Error::Opening` at step 0). Cause: `accumulate` hashes the full encoding of every folded accumulator; at genesis the circuit scaled the previous-proof accumulator by zero but kept its parsed bases, while `next_acc` folded `trivial_acc`. Fix: collapse the previous-proof accumulator after `scale_by_bit`, so at genesis it equals `trivial_acc`, and collapse it off circuit to match. This is in effect realization (b); its justification is still owed here. A completeness bug, not a soundness hole (MockProver: all gates held, 16 instance-copy failures on the accumulator lanes). Node now 652,364 rows (k=20, was 690,682); `gp_fold_and_key` and `sherlock_ivc` pass with 3 stand-in leaves; regression test `tests/ivc_node_mock.rs`. The k=19 of SHKIVC03 was never proven end to end. Input 2026-11-09 (Gemini Quint check, `qa/gemini-quint/ivc/REPORT.md`, 9 of 10 model tests pass): the SHKIVC05 `proof_acc` collapse is sound and matches the off-circuit collapse. Two open items are confirmed by counterexamples in the model: no range checks on `prev_h`, `steps` or `h` (SRC-004: `h` can wrap to 0 mid-chain and set `is_genesis`), and `prev_acc` is folded unscaled and unconstrained at genesis (SRC-005). The CEX-3 cancellation holds in the algebraic model only, because the fold challenge hashes `prev_acc`. The constraint or the written argument is still owed. The lane's proposed hardening fails its own model test (`hardenedTask23SoundAndCompleteTest`), so it is not validated. Input 2026-11-09 (`bd7703f4d`, council S1/S4/S5 formal fixes): cite `genesis_collapse_both` (Aggregation.lean; collapse-after-scale law `collapse_scale_false` replaces `scale_false`), not `genesis_scale_by_bit`; `lin_refines_chain` maps the linear node statement to the F21 chain; `src004_height_bridge` is the range-check contract (raw prev_h, steps, h < 2^64). F21 runner 90 theorems, no sorry, no new axioms (run `20261109T234314Z-F21-lean`); F20 108 pass, 18 of 18 mutants caught incl. PlacementLR and GenesisCarry (`20261109T235258Z-F21-f20`); IVC model 10 of 10 incl. `hardenedTask23SoundAndCompleteTest` (`20261109T235503Z-F21-ivc`). Model evidence, not circuit evidence. Note 2026-11-09 (task 2.3 loop, node `SHKIVC06`, `9189209f0`, `1c2122db7`; not ticked): **Genesis: realization (a), per the S1 lead decision.** The previous-proof accumulator is scaled by `not_genesis` and collapsed (as in SHKIVC05); the carried accumulator is constrained to the `trivial_acc` encoding at genesis (`constrain_genesis_neutral`, every lane of its public encoding, the same lanes `accumulate` hashes at `midnight-circuits 7.3.0`) and to collapsed form at every height (`constrain_collapsed_carry`: scalar one per side, so `collapse c = c`); the host `next_acc` refuses both cases too. The circuit therefore realizes `nodeFold b p c l = collapse (accumulate [collapse (scale b p), collapse (scale b c), l])` on every accepted witness, and `genesis_collapse_both` is the genesis lemma (`collapse (scale false c) = trivial`; the circuit accepts only `c = trivial` there). Why not a literal second collapse of `c`: an in-circuit `collapse` is a variable-base MSM (`collapse_self` measures 239,577 rows); the constraints cost 2,106 rows with the carry assignment and need no new argument. **Heights:** `constrain_heights` checks raw `prev_h < 2^64`, `steps - 1 < S_MAX` (`1 <= steps <= S_MAX`, `S_MAX = 16` provisional, a relation constant) and `h = prev_h + steps < 2^64`, the contract of `src004_height_bridge`. The linear node statement is kept (`lin_refines_chain`). **Negatives (MockProver, each with a passing baseline; `tests/ivc_node_mock.rs`):** genesis steps=2 and steps=S_MAX pass; steps=17 and steps=0 refused; a well-formed non-neutral genesis carry refused (14 copy failures), host refuses it; an invalid genesis leaf satisfies the node and fails the final pairing (stand-in leaf, and under the real node key); step 1 honest passes; `h = 2^64` refused; the CEX-1 wrap (`prev_h = -2`, `steps = 2`, field `h = 0`) refused; a non-collapsed carry of the same value (B/2, scalar 2) refused (2 copy failures). Runs `SHK23-mock-genesis2` and `SHK23-step1-neg2`, exit 0. **End to end:** `gp_fold_and_key` with 3 stand-in leaves: node k=20, three folds (64-67 s each), decider keyed and proved, bundle accepted (`SHK23-gp-chain2`, exit 0, peak 17.6 GB). **k=19 cut: not reachable; node stays at k=20, recorded for G-A.** T1 check: `SherlockIvcRelation::new(4, 19, leaf_vk)` gives `cost_model(&r, Some(19)).k == 20` (rows 652,433; `SHK23-ivccost`). Rows 652,364 (SHKIVC05) -> 652,437 (SHKIVC06, +73 for the fixes); excess over 2^19 is 128,145 (24%). Per-gadget report (`tools/profile` `node_rows`, probe equal to the node, `SHK23-noderows2`), nr_pow2range_cols 4: own_key_and_state 18, carried_acc 2,106, prepare_self 55,788, collapse_self 239,577, prepare_leaf 26,149, accumulate 59,339, collapse_final 267,514, publish 1,946. The two collapses are 78% of the node. Candidates (`prover.md` §2): nr_pow2range_cols 3 measures 877,523 rows (+225k, worse: collapse_self 330,026, collapse_final 395,638); dropping `rule` from the leaf instance is about -100 rows (`binding` struck, SRC-001); the accumulator assignment is 2,106 rows in all. None closes 128k without an architecture change (fewer variable bases in the collapses, the unreleased gadget T6, or S and the tree carrying the target). **Done 2026-11-09** (`bbbfac0a0`, node SHKIVC06): range checks on raw prev_h, steps, h (< 2^64, 1 <= steps <= S_MAX = 16); genesis realization (a) plus a collapsed-form constraint on the carried accumulator at every height, so the circuit equals the Lean `nodeFold` (lead accepts this form 2026-11-09: it is stronger than the brief and costs about 0 rows; a literal second in-circuit collapse would cost about 240k rows). Negatives at each boundary and through the final pairing pass; `gp_fold_and_key` end to end passes (folds 64-67 s, 17.6 GB). **k stays 20**: 652,437 rows, 128,145 over 2^19; the two collapses are 78% of the node; prover.md §2 candidates close at most about 100 rows. Recorded for G-A, which owns the k outcome; S and the tree carry the target.
