   152	    /// Returns which outputs were skipped in the proof preimage, and how many
   153	    /// zero element to buffer them with. Specifically, because our circuits
   154	    /// compile to JavaScript, and there do not evaluate untaken branches, this
   155	    /// leads to the output of the JavaScript circuit targets omitting public
   156	    /// inputs that occurred in an untaken branch. This information still needs
   157	    /// to be included in the statement vectors, where it is padded with zero
   158	    /// elements.
   159	    ///
   160	    /// Currently, we handle this by grouping the statement vector into 'blocks'
   161	    /// of public inputs, with each block corresponding to exactly one VM
   162	    /// instruction, and running `check` to figure out which blocks were
   163	    /// omitted due to untaken branches, and how many zeros to pad them with.
   164	    ///
   165	    /// Long-term, we probably want to move to make this obsolete, by having the
   166	    /// computer target gather information about untaken branches at run-time.
   167	    fn check(&self, preimage: &ProofPreimage) -> Result<Vec<Option<usize>>, ProvingError>;
