    40	## 1. Findings, ranked
    41	
    42	### F1. The tree's gain is parallelism only; total work is unchanged (SOURCE + ESTIMATE)
    43	
    44	`stagenet-gp-recursion.md:167`: "Node count is #leaves-1" for a tree; the linear chain has one
    45	node per leaf. With the slot node (one leaf per node) the count is exactly L nodes for L leaves,
    46	the same as the linear chain. So on a serial lock the tree is worth 0×. The whole case rests on
    47	running P nodes at once. P is bounded by:
    48	
    49	- memory: 26.2 GB peak per k=20 node (`:190-193`); 120 GB host; ESTIMATE P_mem = floor(100/26.2) = 3
    50	  with 20 GB left for the OS, leaf prover and scheduler; 4 if 105 GB is allowed.
    51	- cores: unknown thread count behind the 95 s figure (open question Q1). The A-set checks pin
    52	  `RAYON_NUM_THREADS=4` (`scripts/qa/check-a3.sh:6` and siblings). If 95 s was a 4-thread run,
    53	  five nodes fit the 20 cores at full speed. The recl9 node historically averaged 268 % CPU
    54	  (`wiki-llm/recursion-perf/clusters/s7-recursion/wave-1/FINDINGS.md`, baseline table), so a
    55	  PLONK node of this shape leaves most cores idle most of the time.
    56	- the SRC-011 clause "under 48 GB peak": at 26.2 GB per node this allows P=1. The tree cannot
    57	  pay off without amending that clause to an aggregate cap (§2, task T2).
    58	
    59	### F2. One uniform node key covers every level (SOURCE)
    60	
    61	`ivc.rs:295-301` already takes the node's own key as a public input
    62	(`assign_vk_as_public_input`), and `inner.rs:277-316` (`verify_children_incircuit`) already
    63	verifies several children under one assigned key with one `accumulate` and one collapse. A node
    64	that verifies two self children is those two patterns combined: one `AssignedVk`, two
    65	`verifier.prepare` calls, one `accumulate`. No key family is needed. The decider keeps pinning one
    66	`vk_N_repr` (`run_decider.rs:206`).
    67	
    68	### F3. Accumulator merging is already associative-by-construction in midnight-circuits (SOURCE)
    69	
    70	`midnight-circuits-7.3.0/src/verifier/accumulator.rs:206-225` (`Accumulator::accumulate`): the
    71	challenge r is Poseidon over all input encodings, inputs are weighted by r^i, and
    72	`msm.rs:185-200` (`accumulate_with_r`) merges the named fixed-base scalars by name
    73	(`entry(key).and_modify(|e| *e += r*value)`). "The resulting acc will satisfy the invariant iff
    74	all the accumulators individually do." So a node can fold, in one call:
    75	`[proof_acc_L, carried_L, proof_acc_R, carried_R, leaf_acc]`, with the self fixed-base scalars of
    76	both children left unresolved (as `ivc.rs:13-15` does today) and resolved once by the decider
    77	(`run_decider.rs:217-245`). The grouping is not literally associative (r depends on the group),
    78	but soundness holds for any tree shape, and the off-circuit mirror (`ivc.rs:205-239 next_acc`)
    79	must replay the exact grouping, which is why the tree shape must be part of the bundle (F8).
    80	
