Two GP-3 gaps are now clear in the sources: the recursive gadget uses Poseidon, while ledger contract proofs use Blake2b; and its “public verifying key” leaves the circuit architecture fixed off-circuit. A registry hash alone would not make it a verifier for arbitrary admitted circuits. I’m separating those issues from the recursion primitive and from DAG accounting.
