My recommendation is to test a binary self-recursive node with bounded VM work executed directly inside it. The recorded two-self-proof probe is 730,243 rows; the rejected node added a third, separate leaf proof. That offers a plausible k=20 path, but it still needs hardened disabled-slot handling and a full decider measurement. I’ll keep those as explicit acceptance gates and treat a different inner proof system as the fallback if either fit or throughput fails.
